[0.080, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[3G\u001b[1mWhat changed in Manifest (\u001b[38;2;177;185;249m9dd0d81\u001b[39m):\r\u001b[1B\u001b[22m  - \u001b[1mClean stop:\u001b[22m on\u001b[20GSIGINT\u001b[27Gor\u001b[30GSIGTERM\u001b[38Gthe\u001b[42Gserver\u001b[49Gstops\u001b[55Gtaking\u001b[62Grequests,\u001b[72Gruns\u001b[77Gthe\u001b[81Gones\u001b[86Git\u001b[89Galready\u001b[97Gaccepted\u001b[106Gin\u001b[109Gone\u001b[113Glast\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bstep, answers them and wri\u001b[32Ges\u001b[35Ga snapshot. B\u001b[49Gfore, a request acc\u001b[69Gp\u001b[71Ged just befo\u001b[84Ge the stop got a receipt and\u001b[113Gnever\u001b[119Gan\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Banswer. A restar\u001b[22G now loads\u001b[33Gthat snapshot and repl\u001b[56Gys no\u001b[63Ging.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mBackups:\u001b[22m with \u001b[38;2;177;185;249m--serve --backups <dir>\u001b[39m, a backup is written every time a snapshot is (hourly, and at each stop).\u001b[117GThe\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bdirectory must be\u001b[23Goutside\u001b[31Gthe\u001b[35Gworld's,\u001b[44Gand\u001b[48Gthe\u001b[52Gnewest\u001b[59G24\u001b[62Gbackups\u001b[70Gare\u001b[74Gkept.\u001b[80GA\u001b[82Gbackup\u001b[89Ginterrupted\u001b[101Gbefore\u001b[108Gits\u001b[112Glast\u001b[117Gfile\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bcounts as no backup and is cleared next time. A failed backup is logged and the server keeps running.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mRestore:\u001b[22m \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mmanifest … --restore <backup> --world <dir>\u001b[39m only restores into an empty directory. It refuses a backup\u001b[117Gmade\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bby another build before writing anything. It checks every file and then recovers the world the way a server start\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bdoes. If any of that fails it removes what it wrote. The backup itself is only read.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mStorage limit:\u001b[22m a snapshot bigger than a start can read (4 GiB) is now refused when written, not discovered at\u001b[115Gthe\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bnext start.\u001b[17GThe\u001b[21Gserver\u001b[28Gexits\u001b[34Gwith\u001b[39Gan\u001b[42Gerror\u001b[48Gand\u001b[52Gthe\u001b[56Gworld\u001b[62Gkeeps\u001b[68Gits\u001b[72Glast\u001b[77Ggood\u001b[82Gsnapshot.\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mTests:\u001b[22m th\u001b[14Ghost\u001b[19Gsuite\u001b[25Gcovers\u001b[32Gthe\u001b[36Gstop,\u001b[42Gbackup\u001b[49Gretention\u001b[59Gand\u001b[63Gan\u001b[66Ginterrupted\u001b[78Gbackup,\u001b[86Grestore\u001b[94Gand\u001b[98Gits\u001b[102Grefusals,\u001b[112Gthe\u001b[116Gsize\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Blimit, and a backup di\u001b[27Gct\u001b[30Gry inside the world. A\u001b[53Gnew trading-fixture case\u001b[78Gbacks up a world mid-flight\u001b[106Gwith\u001b[111Ga\u001b[113Gbuy\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Border\u001b[9Gholding\u001b[17Gescrow.\u001b[25GIt\u001b[28Grestores\u001b[37Git,\u001b[41Gchecks\u001b[48Gevery\u001b[54Grequest\u001b[62Goutcome\u001b[70Gmatches,\u001b[79Gand\u001b[83Gflies\u001b[89Gon\u001b[92Gto\u001b[95Gthe\u001b[99Gloop's\u001b[106Gusual\u001b[112Gend\r\u001b[1B \u001b[3Gstate.\u001b[10G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mcli_serve\u001b[39m now restores\u001b[33Gthe s\u001b[39Gop's backup at the step the server stopped,\u001b[83Gand\u001b[87Gchecks\u001b[94Gthat\u001b[99Grestoring\u001b[109Gover\u001b[114Ga\u001b[116Glive\r\u001b[1B  world is refused.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B \u001b[3G\u001b[1mMeasured in Debug:\u001b[22m a backup is 730 KB today. A restore takes\u001b[64G0.25\u001b[69Gs,\u001b[72G0.11\u001b[77Gs\u001b[79Gof\u001b[82Gwhich\u001b[88Gis\u001b[91Gstart-up.\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
