[0.009, "o", "\u001b[H\r\u001b[5B←  ☒ Runtime \u001b[48;2;177;185;249m\u001b[38;2;0;0;0m ☐ TUI \r\u001b[2C\u001b[2B\u001b[49m\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m\u001b[1mS\u001b[5Gould the TUI client be part of the distr\u001b[46Gbution? Right now it\u001b[67Greads its content from a source-tre\u001b[103G \u001b[105Gath compiled \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Binto it, writes its log\u001b[27Gto ./build/, and links libvulkan.so.1 through the engine's\u001b[86Gimgui\u001b[92Gtarget even though \u001b[112Gt never \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bdraws anything.\r\u001b[6C\u001b[2B\u001b[22m\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mhip it (Recommended)\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mShip the server, validator, toke\u001b[39G CLI and TUI. Manifest finds the content next to the executable and logs under XDG\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bstat\u001b[11G. The engine splits\u001b[31GImGu\u001b[36G's GLFW/Vulkan backends out of the imgui targ\u001b[82Gt, \u001b[86Go\u001b[88GDev\u001b[92Gools stops\u001b[103Gl\u001b[106Gking Vulkan. \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mThat\u001b[11Gis\u001b[14Gone engi\u001b[23Ge provision, done before R07.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m2.\u001b[6G\u001b[39mServer tools only\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B  \u001b[6G\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mShip manifest, manifest-validate and manifest-token. The TUI stays a development tool for now, and there is no \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bengine edit.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m3. Typ\u001b[10G something.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m4.\u001b[6GChat about this\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mEnter to select · Tab/Arrow keys to navigate · Esc to cancel\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B\u001b[K\u001b[27;1H\u001b[12;1H"]
