[0.032, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mReading\u001b[11GManifest's\u001b[22GR06\u001b[26Grequirements\u001b[39Gand\u001b[43Gprobing\u001b[51Gthe\u001b[55Grelease\u001b[63Gbinary's\u001b[72Gruntime\u001b[80Gdependencies\u001b[93Gbefore\u001b[100GI\u001b[102Gpropose\u001b[110Gthe\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bdistribution contract.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B \u001b[3G\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mSearched for \u001b[1m5\u001b[22m patterns, read \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m file, listed \u001b[1m2\u001b[22m directories, ran \u001b[1m12\u001b[22m shell commands · \u001b[38;2;255;107;128m1 failed\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mI\u001b[5Ghave\u001b[10Gwhat\u001b[15GR06\u001b[19Gneeds.\u001b[26GThe\u001b[30Gone\u001b[34Greal\u001b[39Gchoice\u001b[46Gis\u001b[49Gwhich\u001b[55Gruntime\u001b[63Gcontract\u001b[72Gto\u001b[75Gsupport,\u001b[84Gso\u001b[87GI'm\u001b[91Gasking\u001b[98Gyou\u001b[102Gbefore\u001b[109GI\u001b[111Gwrite\u001b[117Git\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bup.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mAnswered Claude's questions:\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  · Which runtime distribution should R06 commit Manifest to? Today the release binaries take their interpreter and \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1BRUNPATH from the devenv shell's Nix store paths, and they need glibc symbols up to 2.43, because nixpkgs' glibc is \r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m2.44. → Standalone bundle (Recommended)\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m     \u001b[8G\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mS\u001b[10Gould the TUI client be part of the distr\u001b[51Gbution? Right now it\u001b[72Greads its content from a source-tre\u001b[108G \u001b[110Gath \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mcompiled into it, writes its log to\u001b[42G./build/, and links libvulkan.so.1 through the\u001b[89Gengine's imgui target even \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u00